  "id": "Compound::DB00679 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Thioridazine, an antipsychotic agent, is implicated in the inhibition of Cyp2c9 through multiple mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Thioridazine may act as a causal agent for conditions such as pregnancy test false positives and opisthotonus, both of which are associated with Ondansetron or Perphenazine, which in turn bind to Cyp2c9. This indicates that Thioridazine may indirectly influence Cyp2c9 activity via the pharmacological effects of its metabolites or co-administered drugs. The shared ancestry of Thioridazine with phenothiazines and agents affecting the nervous system further supports a common biological pathway. The integration of these findings implies that Thioridazine may modulate Cyp2c9 expression or activity through a mechanism involving drug-induced changes in enzyme function, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
